-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  linux_elf_archive.adam - x86_64-linux-gnu's ELF reading (Adam.Elf.Reader,
  imported from the compiler's own src\, beside bin\) and its static
  library (Adam.Elf.Format over Adam.Backend.Archive's Gnu kind): an object
  ElfFormat writes is read back (sections with their relocations and
  group, symbols, relocations, as readelf -aW reads the same bytes);
  ReadSection / ReplaceSection on its Info section (a compiled unit's
  payload, H4) and their refusals; two objects (one with a name past 15
  bytes: the long-name table) written as lib<name>.a, read back by
  ReadStaticLibrary byte for byte and dumped entry by entry (as ar t / nm
  -s read it); the shipped linux vendor archives (args: libzlib.a, libc.a)
  read whole, every member through ReadElfObject (counts as readelf / nm
  give them); damaged objects reported (EO0001). The object and the archive
  are also written beside the program (linux_elf_archive.o / .a) for the
  devbox proof: readelf, ar, nm, gcc linking the archive (PLAN-LINUX64 LX2b)
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind run
  args "<BIN>/res/libs/vendor/x86_64-linux-gnu/libzlib.a" "<BIN>/res/libs/vendor/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.a"
  exitcode 0
  | object type 1 machine 0x3E flags 0 sections 13 symbols 7 first global 1 relocs 2
  | [0] '' type 0 flags 0x0 size 0 data no link 0 info 0 align 0 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [1] '.group' type 17 flags 0x0 size 8 data yes link 10 info 5 align 4 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 1
  | [2] '.text' type 1 flags 0x6 size 4 data yes link 0 info 0 align 16 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [3] '.text' type 1 flags 0x6 size 15 data yes link 0 info 0 align 16 relocs 0+1 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [4] '.data' type 1 flags 0x3 size 8 data yes link 0 info 0 align 8 relocs 1+1 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [5] '.bss' type 8 flags 0x3 size 4 data no link 0 info 0 align 4 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [6] '.text' type 1 flags 0x206 size 6 data yes link 0 info 0 align 16 relocs 0+0 group 1 groupflags 0
  | [7] '.adam' type 1 flags 0x80000000 size 4 data yes link 0 info 0 align 1 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [8] '.rela.text' type 4 flags 0x40 size 24 data yes link 10 info 3 align 8 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [9] '.rela.data' type 4 flags 0x40 size 24 data yes link 10 info 4 align 8 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [10] '.symtab' type 2 flags 0x0 size 168 data yes link 11 info 1 align 8 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [11] '.strtab' type 3 flags 0x0 size 59 data yes link 0 info 0 align 1 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | [12] '.shstrtab' type 3 flags 0x0 size 79 data yes link 0 info 0 align 1 relocs 0+0 group 0 groupflags 0
  | sym 0 '' bind 0 type 0 vis 0 shndx 0 value 0 size 0
  | sym 1 'lx2b_add' bind 1 type 2 vis 0 shndx 2 value 0 size 0
  | sym 2 'lx2b_call' bind 1 type 2 vis 0 shndx 3 value 0 size 0
